    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e327003e_38cc68b5",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1526,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T19:58:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having `param` as a key imposes a restriction that two listeners cannot share the same `param.` I\u0027m not sure if there would ever be such a scenario, but should we instead return an opaque pointer to the listener structure we allocated in `wrapfd_add_listener()` and just take that in `wrapfd_del_listener()`?\n\nThat also has the advantage of saving us an O(n) search through the listeners list.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1526,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1526,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "235c792e27289180186993e7e4e80ea64f92c6dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9407bb2_1d38b3bf",
        "filename": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1526,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-04T16:52:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack on the first point but using the opaque pointer as a listener without actually verifying its validity sounds risky to me. I prefer to conduct this O(n) search to confirm it\u0027s a valid listener and only then remove it.",
      "parentUuid": "e327003e_38cc68b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1526,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1526,
        "endChar": 33
      },
